toreProxies.delete(proxy);\n    };\n    const proxy = new Proxy(target, {\n        get(t, prop, receiver) {\n            ensure();\n            return Reflect.get(t, prop, receiver);\n        },\n        has(t, prop) {\n            ensure();\n            return Reflect.has(t, prop);\n        },\n        ownKeys(t) {\n            ensure();\n            return Reflect.ownKeys(t);\n        },\n        getOwnPropertyDescriptor(t, prop) {\n            ensure();\n            return Reflect.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(t, prop);\n        },\n        set(t, prop, value, receiver) {\n            ensure();\n            return Reflect.set(t, prop, value, receiver);\n        },\n        deleteProperty(t, prop) {\n            ensure();\n            return Reflect.deleteProperty(t, prop);\n        },\n        defineProperty(t, prop, desc) {\n            ensure();\n            return Reflect.defineProperty(t, prop, desc);\n        },\n    });\n    droppedContentStoreProxies.add(proxy);\n    return proxy as unknown as MessageContentStore;\n}\n\n/** One successful compress, recorded for #189 observability: correlating a\n *  downstream transient upstream rejection (e.g. GLM 3007 captcha) with the\n *  context rewrite that preceded it. `shrinkRatio` (#1911) is the fraction of\n *  the CURRENT request's live context removed by this compress — counted with\n *  the kernel's own per-message counter over the folded view (capped at 1),\n *  never derived from the billed usage baseline, which can be stale-netted,\n *  clobbered by concurrent streams, or absent after an aborted turn;\n *  `foldPoint` is the start ref of the earliest folded range (where the prefix\n *  structure rewrites). */\nexport type LastCompressInfo = {\n    at: number;\n    shrinkRatio: number;\n    foldPoint: string;\n    blocks: number;\n    tokensCompressed: number;\n};\n\n/** Compact suffix for retry/error logs: the rewrite that may have triggered a\n *  transient upstream rejection. Empty when no compress has been recorded. */\nexport function lastCompressSuffix(info: LastCompressInfo | undefined): string {\n    if (!info) return \"\";\n    return ` [after compress: shrink ${Math.round(info.shrinkRatio * 100)}% foldPoint=${info.foldPoint} blocks=${info.blocks} ~${info.tokensCompressed}tok]`;\n}\n\n/** [#1343] Queued full-text retrieval. `injection` is the ephemeral carrier\n *  (never persisted); ref/tokens/chars/queuedAt back the durable\n *  undelivered-ledger + TTL + drop logging. Lifecycle: queued → attached →\n *  delivered | dropped (see store.ts). */\nexport type PendingRetrieval = {\n    ref: string;\n    tokens: number;\n    chars: number;\n    queuedAt: number;\n    injection: CoreMessage;\n    /** CCR acp_retrieve riders carry the delivery ledger/TTL/counters; other ephemeral carriers (e.g. range restore #1207) only ride along and are removed at the delivery outcome. */\n    ccr?: boolean;\n};\n\nexport type Session = {\n    /** 派生缓存随会话释放，供驻留字节计量遍历；不进入持久化投影或 wire。 */\n    transient?: {\n        pluginMessages?: { processed: CoreMessage[]; original: CoreMessage[]; nudge?: NudgeDecision };\n        sentBody?: SeamSlot;\n        settledBody?: SeamSlot;\n        /** #3023 (cache-ledger): the CLIENT's resent message list of the\n         *  in-flight request (per-message fingerprints + role/len/class meta,\n         *  never raw content), paired at settle like sentBody/settledBody so\n         *  detectSeam can attribute a mid-history break to the client vs to\n         *  bili's rebuild. */\n        inBody?: InboundSlot;\n        settledInBody?: InboundSlot;\n        /** #4805: the conversation's latest ADMITTED message id — the single\n         *  needle the settle-side membership probe tests each resent history\n         *  against. Updated only by member / first-turn / main-scale\n         *  requests, so a foreign payload can neither pass nor hijack it.\n         *  In-memory only; a restart replants it on the first turn. */\n        latestKnownMsgId?: string;\n        needlePayloadUpper?: number;\n        /** #4805: the in-flight request's probe verdict ({member, needle}),\n         *  recorded at prepare and consumed by settleUsageReport. */\n        requestMembership?: { member: boolean; needle: string | null };\n        /** #5293: the user aborted (Esc'd) the model stream mid-turn. The\n         *  interrupted turn's partial output never reports usage, so the next\n         *  usage-grade reading jumps by exactly that unreported mass — counted\n         *  as organic growth, the cadence nudge fires on the user's redirect\n         *  turn (pi: esc → continue → immediate compress injection). `anchor`\n         *  is the meter value at abort time; consumed by the first nudge\n         *  decision whose meter moved past it (absorbAbortedTurnGrowth).\n         *  In-memory only: the abort→resume causality spans one process\n         *  lifetime, and a restart replants nothing. */\n        abortReanchor?: { anchor: number; at: number };\n        /** The upstream rejected a request that carried a nudge: its stamps were\n         *  rolled back, and no nudge rides until a request succeeds (the nudge may\n         *  be what drew the rejection). Cleared by settleUsageReport. */\n        nudgeHeldAfterReject?: boolean;\n        /** #5683/#5943: the conversation's live nudge CREDIT plus the policy\n         *  flags, for the unprompted/out-of-bounds gates (src/unprompted-gate.ts).\n         *  Re-stamped on every prepare (injected rounds re-mint the window,\n         *  un-nudged model rounds decay it); in-memory only — a restart lapses\n         *  any live credit to the all-off default until the first round\n         *  re-stamps, which is safe: no tool call can reach applyRanges before\n         *  its own round's prepare. */\n        unpromptedGate?: UnpromptedGateState;\n        /** #5981: the last model stream on this conversation was CUT before its\n         *  terminal event (src/plugin.ts emitUpstreamTruncation sites). A too